{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2204","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"G. Grid Path"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a grid with $$$n$$$ rows (numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$ from top to bottom) and $$$m$$$ columns (numbered from $$$1$$$ to $$$m$$$ from left to right). You are controlling a chip that is initially in the cell $$$(1, 1)$$$. In one move, the chip can move left, right, or down (if the current cell is $$$(x, y)$$$, it can go to $$$(x, y - 1)$$$, $$$(x, y + 1)$$$, or $$$(x + 1, y)$$$). The chip cannot leave the grid."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can make any number of moves (possibly zero). Let's define the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"path"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of a chip as the set of cells it visits at least once. Note that the order of visited cells "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"doesn't"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" matter."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to calculate the number of possible paths. Since the answer might be large, print it modulo $$$mod$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line contains three integers $$$n$$$, $$$m$$$, and $$$mod$$$ ($$$